# ISS-036 workaround (2026-09-06, Connect Cloud publish prep): forestHelperR
# has "Source": "unknown" in renv.lock (no repository to fetch it from), so
# its .tar.gz is committed here to give it a locally-resolvable source
# without touching renv.lock itself. A negation in the parent .gitignore
# alone can't do this — git won't re-include a file under a directory a
# *closer* .gitignore excludes, so the un-ignore has to live in this file.
!cellar/
!cellar/forestHelperR_0.2.0.tar.gz
